A newsletter signup: a heading, a pitch, a list of perks, an email form with a spam honeypot and a note, and social
links. A **block** composed from [Field](<%= page_path(:field) %>), [Input](<%= page_path(:input) %>),
[Button](<%= page_path(:button) %>) and [Thumbnail](<%= page_path(:thumbnail) %>), as on the
[Appica homepage](https://appica.dev/ui).

<%= embed AppicaUI::Blocks::NewsletterPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Newsletter(action: subscriptions_path, socials: [
  { href: "https://x.com/acme", icon: :brand_x, label: "X" },
  { href: "https://github.com/acme", icon: :brand_github, label: "GitHub" }
]) do
  NewsletterPerk(icon: :sparkles) { "Major library updates" }
  NewsletterPerk(icon: :template) { "Premium templates" }
end
```

- The form posts `email` to `action:` (Turbo submits it, with the CSRF token). The browser validates the address
  first and the Field shows "Enter your email address" / "Enter a valid email address".
- A hidden `website` field (`honeypot:` renames it) catches bots: when it's filled the submission is dropped.
  Check it on the server too.
- After a successful submit the note turns into a thank-you (also announced to screen readers), the field clears
  and `appica-ui--blocks--newsletter:subscribed` fires with `{ email }`.
- Without `action:` the block runs a demo and shows the thank-you at once.
- It has no background of its own - put it on a panel (the preview uses a `dark` one, like Appica's footer).

```ruby
# app/controllers/subscriptions_controller.rb
def create
  head :no_content and return if params[:website].present?

  Subscriber.create_or_find_by!(email: params.require(:email))
  head :ok
end
```

## Localization

`newsletter.locales.yml` holds the title, pitch, note, labels, validation messages and the thank-you (English,
Czech, German, Arabic); `title:`, `description:` and `note:` replace them.

